<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2273" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnestĭa</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμνηστία</span> (a
		forgetting), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an
				amnesty</i>, <i>a forgiving</i> or <i>pardoning of a state crime</i>: haec oblivio, quam
			Athenienses <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμνηστίαν</span> vocant,
					<i><span class="en">Vop. Aur. 39</span></i> (<i><span class="en">Nep.
				Thras. 3, 2</span></i>, uses for it oblivio; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venia et oblivio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abolitio facti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Tib. 4</span></i>
			).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
